    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n23 The Shore is a light-filled and exceptionally spacious detached 4/5-bedroom family home that exudes style, quality and sophistication throughout. Situated within the highly sought-after Marina Village development, this outstanding residence, originally the showhouse, enjoys a prime cul-de-sac setting with breathtaking panoramic views across the Irish Sea, taking in Bray Head, Howth Head and beyond. Combining beautifully appointed contemporary accommodation with an impressive A3 BER rating, this is a home perfectly designed for modern family living.\n\nBuilt to exacting standards, the property offers generous proportions, elegant finishes and a thoughtful layout that maximises both comfort and functionality. Features include impressive 9-foot ceiling heights on the ground floor, luxurious bespoke kitchen cabinetry complemented by quartz worktops, an abundance of natural light throughout the reception and bedroom spaces, and a superb garden room with built-in sauna and home gym. The result is a home of exceptional quality where luxury and practicality combine seamlessly.\n\nUpon entering, a bright and welcoming reception hall, enhanced by rich timber wall panelling, a built-in bench and bespoke cabinetry, immediately sets the tone for the refined interiors that lie beyond. To the front, the beautifully proportioned living room enjoys a large picture window, custom-made alcove cabinetry and a feature log-effect electric fire, creating an inviting space in which to relax.\nTo the rear, the magnificent open-plan kitchen, dining and family room forms the heart of the home. Flooded with natural light through expansive floor-to-ceiling glazing, this impressive space has been designed with both family life and entertaining in mind. The bespoke kitchen is fitted with an extensive range of contemporary cabinetry, a large central island with breakfast bar seating and excellent storage throughout. The dining area is complemented by built-in banquette seating and a feature media wall. A guest WC and practical utility/boot room with side access complete the ground floor accommodation.\n\nOn the first floor, the luxurious principal bedroom suite spans the full width across the back of the home and benefits from a spacious walk-in wardrobe and en suite. To the front, an elegant family room enjoys direct access to a private balcony, perfectly positioned to capture the spectacular uninterrupted sea views stretching from Bray Head to Howth Head. This versatile room could easily be reconfigured as a fifth double bedroom if required. A guest cloakroom with WC and wash hand basin completes this level.\n\nThe second floor provides further superb accommodation, with Bedroom 2 extending across the rear of the house and benefiting from its own en-suite shower room. Bedrooms 3 and 4 are positioned to the front, each enjoying commanding sea views and convenient access to the beautifully appointed family bathroom with bath and separate shower.\nThe rear garden, accessed directly from the kitchen and family room, has been designed as a private and low-maintenance outdoor retreat. Benefiting from a highly desirable south-westerly orientation, it enjoys sunshine throughout the afternoon and evening. An expansive tiled patio and astro turf lawn create an attractive space for outdoor dining and entertaining. To the rear sits a stunning purpose-built garden room, finished in contemporary cladding, with large sliding doors and a skylight flooding the space with natural light. It is fitted out with a built-in sauna, home gym and workstation, and wired with power, TV points and recessed lighting. It offers a private wellness retreat or home office just steps from the house. Additional features include outdoor lighting, external power points, two outdoor taps and secure side access on both sides of the property.\n\nTo the front, the cobble lock driveway provides off-street parking for two cars and includes the added convenience of an EV charging point.\n\nThe location is truly second to none. Marina Village enjoys an enviable position just a short stroll from Greystones Town Centre, the DART station and an exceptional range of sporting and recreational amenities. Nearby facilities include Darcy's Field with its 14-acre park, playground and dog park, Greystones Harbour and Marina, The Cove, South Beach, Shoreline Leisure Centre, Greystones Tennis Club, Rugby Club, Soccer Club, Éire Óg GAA Club and driving range. Several renowned golf clubs and Burnaby Park, with its bowling club, are also within easy reach.\n\nGreystones itself offers an excellent selection of boutiques, cafés, restaurants, supermarkets and a library, alongside superb transport links including the DART, numerous TFI bus services and convenient access to the M11 and M50, placing Dublin City Centre and major business hubs within easy commuting distance. The town is also renowned for its excellent choice of highly regarded primary and secondary schools.\n\nThis award-winning development is recognised for its exceptional build quality and energy-efficient design. With the sea virtually on its doorstep, 23 The Shore offers a rare opportunity to enjoy the very best of coastal living without compromising on modern convenience.\n\nA wonderful place to raise a family and within walking distance of every amenity Greystones has to offer, this exceptional home is sure to appeal to discerning purchasers seeking a contemporary coastal residence of outstanding quality in one of North Wicklow's most desirable locations."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nGround Floor - \n\n\nEntrance Hall - \nWooden flooring, timber wall panelling, bespoke cabinetry incorporating shoe locker and seat.\n\nGuest WC - 1.5m x 1.5m\nTiled floor, partly tiled walls, wc, wash hand basin, recessed lighting, chrome heated towel rail.\n\nLiving Room - 4.1m x 5.45m\nLarge picture window to front, bespoke alcove cabinetry with mirror back, wall-mounted lighting, electric inset fire.\n\nKitchen/Dining/Family Room - 4.34m x 6m\nBespoke cabinetry and shelving with generous quartz countertops, Siemens 5-ring induction hob, extractor fan with lighting, full-size integrated fridge, full-size integrated freezer, Siemens integrated microwave and separate oven, large island/breakfast bar with sink, storage and integrated wine fridge. Built-in banquette seating and media wall with shelving to dining area. Floor-to-ceiling glazing with access to rear garden.\n\nUtility Room - 2.6m x 2.35m\nEye and floor level units, side access, plumbed for washing machine with provision for dryer.\n\nFirst Floor - \n\n\nFamily Room - 5.59m x 3.9m\nBespoke cabinetry and infotainment unit, LED lighting and recessed downlighting. Large sliding door to balcony overlooking the sea with stunning views to Bray Head and beyond\n\nBalcony - 5.7m x 1.88m\nDecked patio area with ample space for outdoor furnishings.\n\nGuest WC - 1.7m x 1.8m\nTiled floor, wash hand basin, wc, marble countertop, fitted vanity mirror and chrome heated towel rail.\n\nMain Bedroom - 3.98m x 5.65m\nLarge double bedroom with custom-designed built-in floor-to-ceiling headboard, wall-mounted lighting, door to large walk-in wardrobe complete with shelving and hanging space\n\nWalk In Wardrobe - \nHaving extensive hanging and shelving space\n\nEn-Suite - 1.7m x 2.9m\nWindow, tiled floor, extensively tiled walls, large fitted mirror, wash hand basin, marble countertops, recessed lighting, large step-in thermostatic shower with rainfall shower head and handheld attachment.\n\nSecond Floor - \n\n\nLanding - \nAccess to store.\n\nBedroom 2 - 5.95m x 5.26m\nLarge double bedroom to rear, built-in wardrobes, fitted built-in bunk beds and desk with storage.\n\nEn-Suite - 2.2m x 1.5m\nStep-in thermostatic shower, wash hand basin, wc, fitted mirror with marble countertops, partly tiled walls, tiled floor and chrome heated towel rail.\n\nBedroom 3/Home Office - 3.4m x 2.9m\nDouble bedroom, built-in wardrobes, sea views.\n\nBedroom 4 - 2.67m x 2.9m\nCurrently in use as a nursery, wall panelling, sea views.\n\nFamily Bathroom - 2.2m x 2.61m\nBath, separate step-in shower with rainfall head, wc, wash hand basin, fitted mirror, tiled floor, partly tiled walls, recessed lighting.\n\nOutside - \n\n\nGarden - \nExpansive tiled patio and astro turf lawn, enclosed by timber fencing. Side access on both sides, one of which is covered, providing valuable additional storage. Outdoor lighting, external power points and two outdoor taps.\n\nGarden Room - 5.57m x 3.3m\nClad exterior, large sliding doors and skylight. Built-in sauna, gym area and workstation. Recessed lighting, power and TV points.\n\nFront - \nCobble lock driveway with off-street parking for two cars. EV charging point.\n\n"
      },
